{
  "name": "walrus",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-06, the sculpt overlay; generator scratchpad sc/sea3/gen/walrus.py): a WALRUS (Odobenus rosmarus), a bull, 3 m muzzle to tail and its hind flippers 0.5 m more, ~1.2 t -- massive but ELONGATED: a spindle, deepest and widest (1.06 m) at the shoulders and chest, about a metre high lying, the back sloping and tapering to a narrow pelvis (the shoulders 1.5x the hips), thick FAT FOLDS round the neck and the bull's knobbly bosses; a SMALL head (a third of the shoulders' width) on a thick folded neck, the outline dipping between them; the MUZZLE a broad flattened squarish pad under a dense MOUSTACHE of stiff pale bristles, the nostrils on top of it, small eyes high on the sides, no ears; the TUSKS, 0.6 m of ivory hanging from the upper jaw. Drawn lying on land: the big paddle FORE FLIPPERS propped forward and out beside the chest, palms on the ground (broad, square-ended, hairless, small nails), the HIND FLIPPERS back, fanned out flat on the ground -- haulout.js turns them FORWARD under the pelvis when it walks, and sweeps the fore flippers back when it swims. Cinnamon-pink-brown, wrinkled, sparse-haired (coatpat.js `walrus`: creases across the folds and a net of them elsewhere, pinker low down and over the chest). In the world: a small herd (or one wanderer) on a sea's shore (haulout.js). (2026-11-08) The TUSKS are one sharp `horn` each (sharp.js): smooth and truly pointed. (2026-11-08, fair_bases.py) The TUSKS' roots are FAIRED into the head (sharp.js horn `fair`): the smooth union of tusk and skin, a gum the body's colour, no crease.",
  "kind": "parts",
